 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 1536,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "First 256 bytes of the unpacked M1 map resource. In the naturally reached closed-gate snapshot, cells zero through three are $01,$03,$01,$01; the shared classifier uses these for the first four 64-unit horizontal columns. The selected gate example covers world X zero through 255. Other map consumers and rows remain open."
  },
  {
   "address": 1854,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen low-nibble-to-type entries read by the shared map classifier. Initially entry one maps to type zero and entry three to type fourteen. The gate approach threshold writes type fourteen into entries zero and two when it starts the sequence. These are mutable scene-map semantics, not a pixel collision rectangle."
  },
  {
   "address": 2105,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "JMP $0A61, the resident counted-delay service. The gate stage at $8CC0 calls this with Y four before queuing the first corridor."
  },
  {
   "address": 2657,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "For each Y count, load A sixty, store/reset IRQ downcounter $030E and call $0A6D until it becomes zero. Decrement Y and repeat until zero. The gate uses Y four, giving four sixty-tick waits. This annotation does not equate an interval to a wall-clock second."
  },
  {
   "address": 2669,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Store A in $030E and busy-wait until the IRQ-maintained downcounter becomes zero, then return. The counted wrapper supplies sixty each time."
  },
  {
   "address": 16753,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Set Y zero and enter $4173. In the negative $0343 map mode, use the player world X pair $0538/$053C to choose a map cell. The gate approach test exercises this entry against all 256 low-coordinate values."
  },
  {
   "address": 16755,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "For negative $0343, shift world X left twice and mask its resulting high byte with $5E to select column $AF. Read $0600,X into $B7, translate its low nibble through $073E to type $B0, and use nonnegative type or fallback zero to load depth bound $B2 and auxiliary byte $B3 from $41F0/$4200. Other modes call room hooks and use $0344; those branches are outside the gate approach example."
  },
  {
   "address": 16880,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen maximum-depth values used by the shared classifier. Type zero has bound $18 (24); type fourteen has bound $FF (255). At the closed gate, ordinary cells have low nibble one, mapped to type zero; column one has low nibble three, mapped to type fourteen."
  },
  {
   "address": 16896,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen auxiliary signed bytes paired with $41F0 for the shared movement code. Type zero has $FF and type fourteen has zero in this image. A depth bound alone does not describe all movement and exit logic."
  },
  {
   "address": 22959,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "If $02C3 is nonnegative and $0530 remains negative, copy the deferred byte into $0530. For a nonzero scene with unspecified $0532=$FF, supply entry one. Clear $02C3 to $FF. When $0530 is nonnegative, call $60E6 and loader $5098. A stopping live store watch observed the corridor-two request at the store ending $59BC."
  },
  {
   "address": 35974,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Three JMP stubs at $8C86/$8C89/$8C8C all target the RTS at $8EA3. The gate normally uses the resident negative-mode map classifier, rather than these alternate classification callbacks."
  },
  {
   "address": 35983,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "JMP $8C96, the gate sequence callback invoked from the resident scene/action loop. It handles the gate story stages and the approach-depth condition."
  },
  {
   "address": 35986,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "JMP the RTS at $8C95. The per-motion room-update callback has no additional body in this gate overlay; the command/frame callback at $8C8F carries its scripted sequence."
  },
  {
   "address": 35989,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Return from the gate update hook. This one-byte RTS is also the target of the $8C92 jump."
  },
  {
   "address": 35990,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Read gate script stage $8ED3. Negative selects the ordinary waiting/dialogue path at $8CD8. Stages zero and one classify the current map cell through API $0818, change it using $072E through API $081B, request sound three through API $081E, disable the player display slot and set depth $C0 before incrementing the stage. Stage at least two enters $8CC0, which queues the first corridor after a counted delay. The approach threshold is separately described at $8D92; other dialogue helpers remain partially analysed."
  },
  {
   "address": 36032,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Request sound five through API $081E, then call API $0839 with Y four, waiting through four sixty-tick downcounter intervals. Store two in deferred scene byte $02C3, end the current object-sequence flag and increment $8ED3. Resident $59AF later transfers the deferred request into $0530; this does not use the generic $4115 exit dispatcher. Tests keep the original counted-delay loop and intercept only its per-interval wait."
  },
  {
   "address": 36242,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Read player depth $0544. Return if its sign bit is set or if it is below $32 (50). Otherwise store zero in gate stage $8ED3 and store type fourteen into mapping entries $073E and $0740. This begins the gate script; there is no horizontal-coordinate comparison inside this routine. Closed-gate map depth limits restrict the approach elsewhere. All 256 depth bytes are tested against this original routine."
  }
 ]
}